      "description": "Next generation Site Controller and Expansion Hub, C++ and object-oriented architecture.\nWorked on the team that developed the hardware abstraction layer, hot-swap capabilities, and various functionalities in the platform.\nDeveloped 802.1x passthrough functionality on Broadcom BCM5380 switch.\nLed development team in updating time reference tuning algorithm to support multiple sources, source signal wellness-checks, and greatly improved signal lock via the implementation of a multi-zone PI controller algorithm which resulted in a tripling of the free-run time.\nSupported services, application, and system test teams' integration with the new platform. \nPrimary subject matter expert for the platform layer for the site controller (comprised of fault management, time reference locking, GPS receiver management, battery charging, embedded Ethernet switch management.\nTechnical lead for the platform layer on the next Next-Gen site controller and the subsequent reduced footprint RF-site module.",
